## Why This Is Asked

Assesses the ability to design a CKNE-aware inference gateway that dynamically allocates shared compute resources across tenants with real-time rebalancing, ensuring SLA adherence and fairness under burst traffic conditions.

## Key Concepts

- **CKNE-to-quotas mapping**: Per-tenant concurrency limits, token budgets, and model selection strategies
- **Real-time degradation loop**: Minute-by-minute capacity reallocation and preemption mechanisms
- **Telemetry and fairness**: SLA monitoring, starvation prevention, resource accounting, and observability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: compute per-tenant max concurrent inferences from CKNE
function quotaForCKNE(ckne, base = 1, max = 8) {
  return Math.floor(base + (max - base) * ckne);
}

// Pseudo: minute-by-minute degradation loop
async function degradationLoop() {
  while (true) {
    const metrics = await gatherTelemetry();
    const overloaded = metrics.utilization > 0.8;

    if (overloaded) {
      await reallocateCapacity(metrics);
    }

    await sleep(60000); // 1 minute
  }
}
```

